  "html": "<h1>DataSet</h1>\n<p>A DataSet holds the working data for an application screen. Its named tables implement\nthe DataSource contract, while DataRow objects retain their identity across edits,\nrollback and undo/redo. Edits are local until the application saves the accumulated changes.</p>\n<p>Use it when several views should share pending edits, calculated fields and one data\nhistory. A remote source can still be used directly; a DataSet is useful when the\napplication wants a local batch-edit workspace.</p>\n<h2 id=\"try-an-order-editor\">Try an order editor</h2>\n<p>The sales order has a header in <code>salesOrders</code> and its lines in <code>salesOrderLines</code>.\nClick <strong>Edit</strong> or <strong>Add line</strong> to open a form. <strong>OK</strong> accepts the form locally;\n<strong>Cancel</strong> discards its input. A business rule calculates the line amount and updates\nthe total in the order header. One <strong>Undo</strong> reverses the accepted edit and both totals.\nDeleting a line also updates the order total and can be undone.</p>\n<p><strong>Save order</strong> sends the accumulated changes to a simulated server. Successful saving\naccepts the data, maps temporary line IDs and clears the data undo history. Under\n<strong>Behind the scenes</strong>, enable <strong>Simulate server rejection</strong> to see a failed save\nretain the local changes. A new line is pending until <strong>OK</strong> inserts it; <strong>Cancel</strong>\ncancels its session. Undoing insertion restores the draft: use <strong>Resume draft</strong> to\nfinish or cancel it before saving.</p>\n<div data-live-demo=\"dataset-order-editor\"></div>\n<p>Expand <strong>Behind the scenes</strong> to inspect the save payload and event log. Business entries\nshow the transaction label, table, row ID and old → new field values, including derived\nline and header totals. Lifecycle entries show the row values; committed UI notifications\nshow the resulting row or table snapshot. Server entries include the request and ID mappings.\nBusiness events (“BEFORE” and “AFTER”) are distinct from committed UI notifications\n(“UI”). Their <code>kind</code> values are listed in\n<a href=\"?!=/data/dataset/rules#event-kinds\">Event kinds</a>. The contracts are\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/DataRowChangeEvent\">DataRowChangeEvent</a> and\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/DataSourceChanged\">DataSourceChanged</a>.</p>\n<p>The form keeps its inputs separate from the working data until <strong>OK</strong>. Editing an\nexisting line and inserting a new one share the same acceptance path:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"background-color:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e;color:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">const</span><span style=\"color:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> result</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> await</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> dataset.</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">transaction</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(</span><span style=\"color:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"Accept order line\"</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">async</span><span style=\"color:#E36209;--shiki-dark:#FFAB70\"> tx</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =></span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    await</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> tx.</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">update</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(lines, row, { product, quantity, price });</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">    if</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (newRowSession) </span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">await</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> tx.</span><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">insert</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(newRowSession);</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">});</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">if</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> (</span><span style=\"color:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\">!</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">result.success) {</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">    showFormError</span><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">(result.error); </span><span style=\"color:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\">// keep the form open for correction</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"color:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">}</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"></span></code></pre>\n<p>API: <a href=\"?!=/api-reference/DataSet#transaction\">DataSet.transaction()</a>,\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/DataTransaction#update\">DataTransaction.update()</a>,\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/DataTransaction#insert\">insert()</a>,\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/NewRowSession\">NewRowSession</a>,\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/MutationResult\">MutationResult</a>.</p>\n<p>Accepting the form does not contact the server. <strong>Save order</strong> later calls\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/DataSet#saveChanges\">DataSet.saveChanges()</a> with the complete\nbatch from both tables. Cancelling an existing-line form needs no rollback because\nits inputs have not been applied; cancelling a new-line form calls\n<a href=\"?!=/api-reference/NewRowSession#cancel\">NewRowSession.cancel()</a>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"related-topics\">Related topics</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"?!=/data/dataset/tables\">Tables, rows and change tracking</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"?!=/data/dataset/rules\">Transactions and business rules</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"?!=/data/dataset/new-rows\">New-row sessions</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"?!=/data/dataset/saving\">Saving, accepting and rejecting changes</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"?!=/data/data-source/caching\">Local processing and cache invalidation</a></li>\n</ul>\n",
